#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9284b0a5-6797-5f77-b7a1-d4c0b8fe315e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338274} {:answer/id #uuid "027c16c5-2973-5717-8af4-0135a10f6020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338275} {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} {:answer/id #uuid "274fc05d-1f82-55d1-bec8-b925b6291c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338277} {:answer/id #uuid "42cfe6cd-8c70-5046-b98e-d974d4d8aea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5df713a-1952-5f2f-aad9-fbc435f9cd6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a435c59-9a38-57a4-9c2b-af498b51b708" :question/math-academy-id "q-17524" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-2+6\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93831ade-92f3-55a1-898c-1fa9b3e39dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2\\sqrt{3}e^{π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086318} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7fafd2-561e-57cf-b458-6ac7b266706e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{5π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086319} {:answer/id #uuid "12a1c4f6-c394-5811-bf5c-ec8f6641bd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3e^{3π\\textrm{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086320} {:answer/id #uuid "2c382927-796b-5057-a3b3-9cad5a5084cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3\\sqrt{2}e^{π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086321} {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322} :answer-field/id #uuid "1736925a-0723-5e18-b493-5324e70cc51b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "145945c1-66ab-5fe7-89d2-3b7864c48fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$"}]}
